<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.216 percent from 10.257 percent at the previous auction on November 5.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: May 13, 1997 (May 6, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.216 percent (10.257)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 992.525 million (545.900 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.28 billion (735.900 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.999-10.247 percent (10.101-10.291)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.999-10.600 percent (10.101-10.600)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 174 (134)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 215 (141)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
